    "measuredAt": "2026-10-19",
    "baseline": "All cases checked in a fresh process in checkout eb81c10d, whose kernel is identical to main 89f73ea1, plus the versioned fixture/probe additions, with the unused semiring import removed. Standard 512 syntax-depth and 1024 native recursion guards retained. Declaration commits clear reduction caches; decimal literal parsing is part of each measured normalization.",
    "diagnostic": "Same fixture sources, kernel 89f73ea1 with only the following temporary syntax-depth guard patch. This was reverted and baseline WASM rebuilt after measurement. No production guard change is part of this PR.",
    "diagnosticPatch": "diff --git a/kernel/src/term_store.c b/kernel/src/term_store.c\nindex 6d666892..0573129c 100644\n--- a/kernel/src/term_store.c\n+++ b/kernel/src/term_store.c\n@@ -239,8 +239,8 @@ cc_term ck_make(cc_kernel *k, cc_term_kind kind, uint32_t payload,\n     for (unsigned i = 0; i < arity; ++i)\n         if (children[i] && k->nodes[children[i]].depth >= depth)\n             depth = k->nodes[children[i]].depth + 1;\n-    if (depth > 512)\n-        return ck_fail_as(k, CC_ERROR_RESOURCE, \"Native prototype syntax depth exceeds 512.\"), 0;\n+    if (depth > 2048)\n+        return ck_fail_as(k, CC_ERROR_RESOURCE, \"Diagnostic syntax depth exceeds 2048.\"), 0;\n     if (k->count >= UINT32_MAX)\n         return ck_fail_as(k, CC_ERROR_RESOURCE, \"Term handle space exhausted.\"), 0;\n     if (k->count >= k->capacity) {\n",
    "notes": "Both logs record modified-tree paths. Failed queries have no complete normal-form size. Timings and process memory are exploratory single samples, not stable benchmark claims. The kernel probe does not test JavaScript decoding/printing; absence of a detected overflow in the diagnostic does not establish that recursive traversals are safe at that enlarged depth."
  },
